[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3861278388","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115964#issuecomment-3861278388","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115964","id":3861278388,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mJm60","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-06T16:17:12Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T16:17:12Z","body":"This will cause stuttering, which kind of defeats the purpose of using background loading. \r\n\r\nThe high priority queue is meant for stuff that needs to executed as soon as possible and will typically be waited on. If you insert a long running background task into the high priority queue, there is a good chance the engine will end up waiting on a task behind it in the queue and stall until your load is finished. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3861278388/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3861537737","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115964#issuecomment-3861537737","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115964","id":3861537737,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mKmPJ","user":{"login":"Rinnegatamante","id":9152710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNTI3MTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9152710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante","html_url":"https://github.com/Rinnegatamante","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-06T16:57:26Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T16:57:57Z","body":"> This will cause stuttering, which kind of defeats the purpose of using background loading.\r\n> \r\n> The high priority queue is meant for stuff that needs to executed as soon as possible and will typically be waited on. If you insert a long running background task into the high priority queue, there is a good chance the engine will end up waiting on a task behind it in the queue and stall until your load is finished.\r\n\r\nThe PR does not push resource load request with high_priority to the high priority pool specifically to avoid stuttering. They will still be sent to low priority pool. The only difference is how they get enqueued in the list. If high_priority is set, it will use `add` else it will use `add_last`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3861537737/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3861647014","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115964#issuecomment-3861647014","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115964","id":3861647014,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mLA6m","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-06T17:15:18Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T17:15:18Z","body":"> The PR does not push resource load request with high_priority to the high priority pool specifically to avoid stuttering. They will still be sent to low priority pool. The only difference is how they get enqueued in the list. If high_priority is set, it will use `add` else it will use `add_last`.\r\n\r\nThanks for the clarification. I definitely wouldn't use the `high_priority` parameter to mean \"low priority but add to front of the low priority queue\".\r\n\r\nSince you are adding a new parameter anyway you should be adding a parameter specifically for that. It is unnecessarily complex to override the behaviour of an existing parameter and then add a new parameter that says \"ignore that previous parameter\" and do something else. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3861647014/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3861719452","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115964#issuecomment-3861719452","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115964","id":3861719452,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mLSmc","user":{"login":"Rinnegatamante","id":9152710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNTI3MTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9152710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante","html_url":"https://github.com/Rinnegatamante","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-06T17:29:35Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T17:30:57Z","body":"I picked the high_priority name solely cause an engine user likely has no full understanding of what goes on underneat when a load_threaded_request call is performed so calling it something like enqueue_on_head would be confusing while high_priority conveys better the actual final result that having such a parameter on would produce.\r\n\r\nWould a name like have_priority or give_priority be good here?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3861719452/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3861795632","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115964#issuecomment-3861795632","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115964","id":3861795632,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mLlMw","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-06T17:46:36Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T17:46:36Z","body":"> I picked the high_priority name solely cause an engine user likely has no full understanding of what goes on underneat when a load_threaded_request call is performed so calling it something like enqueue_on_head would be confusing while high_priority conveys better the actual final result that having such a parameter on would produce.\r\n> \r\n> Would a name like have_priority or give_priority be good here?\r\n\r\nGood question. Something like \"process_this_task_before_other_low_priority_tasks\" would be ideal haha. I think the term \"priority\", while accurate, is too overloaded here. Since the WTP has a concept of priority, and this new feature doesn't actually interact with that concept at all. I think we should avoid calling two distinct properties the same name. Instead I would do something like \"front_of_queue\", or to be even shorter \"queue_front\". ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3861795632/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3863142756","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115964#issuecomment-3863142756","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115964","id":3863142756,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mQuFk","user":{"login":"Rinnegatamante","id":9152710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNTI3MTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9152710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante","html_url":"https://github.com/Rinnegatamante","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rinnegatamante/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-07T00:32:39Z","updated_at":"2026-02-07T00:32:39Z","body":"Renamed the parameter to queue_front and added also a note in documentation for how it works.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3863142756/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3864345065","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115964#issuecomment-3864345065","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115964","id":3864345065,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mVTnp","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/B